spec:
  grid: 15-28 rows x 15-27 cols, uniform background (yellow=4)
  objects:
    count: 3-4 blue(1) 4-connected components on the background
    hollow: 1-2 components have exactly 1 enclosed rectangular hole (4-conn bg region fully inside bbox)
    solid: 1-3 components without enclosed holes
    cell_count: 1-125 per component; hollow >= 10, solid any size
    hole_size: 2-16 cells, always rectangular (1x2 to 4x4)
    shape: |
      irregular polyominoes; each row of the component is NOT necessarily contiguous
      (the hole creates non-contiguous rows). Shapes typically look like a large
      rectangle with 0-2 rectangular corner notches cut away plus an interior
      rectangular hole (for hollow components). Solid components range from single
      cells to large L/T/staircase shapes.
  spacing:
    Chebyshev distance >= 3 between any two components [observed]
    border clearance >= 1 from grid edge (outline may touch row/col 0)
    outlines never overlap each other [observed]
  transform:
    outline: draw 1-cell 8-neighborhood red(2) border around each component on bg cells only
    hollow_recolor: if component has enclosed holes, recolor component to teal(8) and holes to magenta(6) BEFORE outlining
    solid_keep: solid components stay blue(1); outline drawn around them
    hole_inclusion: holes treated as part of solid mask for outline computation

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct input generation (transform is deterministic)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size 15-28 rows x 15-27 cols, fill with bg=4
    2. Choose 3-4 components; designate 1-2 as hollow, rest as solid
    3. For each component, generate an irregular polyomino by union of 2-3 overlapping axis-aligned rectangles (creates L/T/staircase shapes)
    4. For hollow components, carve a rectangular hole (2-16 cells) fully enclosed within the shape interior (ensure >= 1 fg cell on all 4 sides of hole)
    5. Place components on grid with Chebyshev >= 3 pairwise and >= 1 from grid edges
    6. Verify all components are 4-connected and holes are properly enclosed
