    pixels: 4-6 filled out of 9, density 0.44-0.67
    not required to be 4-connected
  markers:
    count: 2-4 single-pixel foreground colors, each appearing exactly once
    alignment: all share one row (horizontal) or one column (vertical), never both
    spacing: evenly spaced with gap=2 along the shared axis [observed]
    colors: distinct non-bg non-template colors (from palette 2-9)
  layout: template and marker line are in separate, non-overlapping regions of the grid
  output:
    horizontal markers -> concat recolored template copies left-to-right, size 3 x (3*N)
    vertical markers -> concat recolored template copies top-to-bottom, size (3*N) x 3
    each copy replaces template pixels with the marker color in sorted order (L-to-R or T-to-B)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is simple enough)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims H,W in [9,14]. Pick N markers in [2,4].
    2. Choose axis = horizontal or vertical.
    3. Generate a random 3x3 binary mask with 4-6 filled cells (at least 1 per row and column to avoid degenerate bbox).
    4. Place the template (color 1) at a random position within the grid where the 3x3 bbox fits.
    5. Choose N distinct marker colors from {2..9} minus {1}.
    6. Pick a shared row (if horizontal) or shared column (if vertical) not overlapping with template bbox rows/columns.
    7. Place markers evenly spaced (gap=2) along the shared axis, ensuring all fit within grid bounds and don't overlap template bbox.
    8. Verify grid is mostly background (>90%) and template + markers don't overlap.
